WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:02.520
Hey guys,
You know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:09.200
the role of a father is extremely important.
More than most men will ever realize.&nbsp;

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:13.160
Unfortunately, they only&nbsp;
realize it when it is too late.&nbsp;

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:16.640
And you can never go back.
You can never make it right again.&nbsp;

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:24.520
We have a fatherless problem in the world today.
And even when fathers are at home, a lot of them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:28.840
are not really present.
Are you?&nbsp;

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:35.480
According to fatherly.com, kids who grow up&nbsp;
with a present, engaged dad are less likely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:42.520
to drop out of school or wind up in jail,&nbsp;
compared to children with absent fathers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:48.800
and no other male caretakers or role models.
When children have close relationships with father&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:54.800
figures they tend to avoid high risk behaviors.
And they're less likely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.800 --> 00:01:00.280
to have sex at a young age.
They're more likely to have high-paying jobs and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:04.520
healthy, stable relationships when they grow up.
You see, the world is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:10.840
downplaying the role of a father.
But the role of a father is extremely important.&nbsp;

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:18.600
Listen to the rest of this: They also tend to&nbsp;
have higher IQ test scores by the age of three,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:23.400
and endure fewer psychological&nbsp;
problems throughout their lives.&nbsp;

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:30.360
When dads take the role of a father seriously,&nbsp;
altogether these benefits of having an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:39.720
engaged dad are called the father effect.
Now, you might not have had a great father.&nbsp;

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:43.840
You know, an example.
But that is no excuse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:49.280
because as with everything in life, you&nbsp;
can always learn and improve yourself.&nbsp;

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:55.760
And there are many things that we can talk about&nbsp;
but I want to focus in on five extremely important&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.760 --> 00:02:03.280
things that can help you to be a better father.
These are things that I experienced with my dad.&nbsp;

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:08.560
A dad who lived the way he preached.
He's not here anymore.&nbsp;

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:11.080
He passed away.
But all those things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:18.920
he taught me changed my life forever.
Let's start with the first thing.

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:26.880
The first thing is: Follow God's Word because that&nbsp;
actually takes everything into account when you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:30.680
want to be a good father.
Even the small things.&nbsp;

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:34.320
For example, the Bible says that&nbsp;
you have to be a man of your word.&nbsp;

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:39.800
That means including, when you&nbsp;
make promises to your children,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:43.080
you should keep them.
That's what my dad did.

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:45.040
[James 5:12]

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:09.080
The biggest thing your child needs&nbsp;
from you is love, but also trust.&nbsp;

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:12.520
Trust.
If you don't keep your promises,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:17.000
if your yes is not yes and your no is not&nbsp;
no, what do you think is going to happen?&nbsp;

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:21.520
They're not going to trust you, right?
And that's just one thing.&nbsp;

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:27.160
In the Word of God - follow God's Word&nbsp;
- and see how it will improve you to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:30.040
become a better father.
Here's another example.

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:31.360
[Proverbs 20:7]

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:44.040
My dad lived according to God's Word&nbsp;
and that automatically made him a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:47.880
man of integrity because he followed God's Word.&nbsp;

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:56.320
And me, being young, all those years growing&nbsp;
up, I saw how my dad lived with integrity.&nbsp;

00:03:56.320 --> 00:03:59.480
That he was a doer of the&nbsp;
Word, and not just a hearer.&nbsp;

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:06.280
And today, I am blessed after him because&nbsp;
I saw all his decisions - experiences - and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:12.960
actions - how he walked in integrity.
And I will never forget it.&nbsp;

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:16.520
Now, if you don't know God's&nbsp;
Word, then it is time to learn it.

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:17.960
[Psalm 119:105]

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:29.600
The world is full of darkness, as&nbsp;
your children will also experience,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:35.480
but if you stay there in the darkness&nbsp;
trying to lead them, you will stumble.&nbsp;

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:39.440
You'll be lost.
And you will also cause them to be lost.&nbsp;

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:43.680
And that is where you will&nbsp;
stay - in darkness forever.&nbsp;

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:50.160
You need God's Word to be a lamp for your feet&nbsp;
on this earthly temporary journey so that you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:58.000
can see the truth for yourself and walk towards&nbsp;
the destiny - the purpose - that God has for you.&nbsp;

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:04.520
If you follow God and His Word, God will bless&nbsp;
you, equip you with everything you need to take on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:09.760
every obstacle that this life throws at you.
And you know, sometimes it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:14.320
is not easy to raise children.
But God will help you with that as well.

00:05:14.320 --> 00:05:15.960
[2 Timothy 3:16]

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:43.840
All of us - we are born as human&nbsp;
beings with a sinful nature.&nbsp;

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:48.240
Your kids - you never have to tell&nbsp;
them to be naughty - they just are.&nbsp;

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:49.800
Why?&nbsp;

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:54.160
Because of the sinful nature&nbsp;
in us that we are born with.

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:54.760
David said:

00:05:54.760 --> 00:05:56.920
[Psalm 51:5}

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:10.360
Now, when we become reborn Christians,&nbsp;
we receive a new spiritual nature.&nbsp;

00:06:10.360 --> 00:06:12.840
The Holy Spirit, right?
So we have that nature.&nbsp;

00:06:12.840 --> 00:06:16.880
We also still have that old sinful flesh.
And when we act through the Spirit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:20.680
we will not sin.
This new nature helps us to overcome sin.&nbsp;

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:25.880
But when we don't act through the Spirit,&nbsp;
when we act through the flesh, we will sin.&nbsp;

00:06:25.880 --> 00:06:31.480
We will fall and so not only not only&nbsp;
do we receive the new spiritual nature,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.480 --> 00:06:37.080
we also become children of God.
He adopts us after He declared us as righteous.&nbsp;

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:43.200
But that doesn't mean that when we sin, He will&nbsp;
just think okay, that's fine, and just leave it.&nbsp;

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:48.400
He disciplines us as a good&nbsp;
father because He loves us.

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:49.520
[Revelation 3:19]

00:06:53.720 --> 00:07:03.560
And in the same way if you truly&nbsp;
love your children, you will also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:09.120
discipline them if they are naughty or do evil.
Because if you don't, you're basically teaching&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:15.480
them that they can do evil, sinful things&nbsp;
with no consequences, so it's fine, go ahead.

00:07:15.480 --> 00:07:17.200
[Proverbs 22:15]

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:29.600
So if you don't discipline&nbsp;
them, they will think they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.600 --> 00:07:34.040
can always get what they want, when they want.
They don't care who they hurt ... they can just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.040 --> 00:07:40.080
do whatever and they will get their desires.
No one stops me.&nbsp;

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:43.480
There's no consequences.
So why not, and then they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:46.840
become extremely selfish.
And that's how they grow up.&nbsp;

00:07:46.840 --> 00:07:51.760
And that's how they become - these mature men&nbsp;
and women walking around who are extremely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.760 --> 00:07:56.040
selfish and just care about themselves.
So if you don't care - if you don't truly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.040 --> 00:08:01.600
love your kids and you don't discipline them&nbsp;
- then this is what might happen to them.&nbsp;

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:06.960
So if you love them and truly care&nbsp;
about them, you will discipline them.

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:08.600
[Proverbs 13:24]

00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:21.640
So think about it this way.
If you don't discipline them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:29.240
you actually nurture that sinful fleshly nature&nbsp;
of them even more and more so when they grow up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.240 --> 00:08:31.840
they don't really care that much&nbsp;
about right and wrong anymore.&nbsp;

00:08:31.840 --> 00:08:35.600
They're a bad husband, a bad father.
They do sleep around.&nbsp;

00:08:35.600 --> 00:08:39.520
They do whatever they want at work.
They steal, they bribe, they do whatever they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:44.120
want, because that's how you taught them.
It's okay, there's no consequences.

00:08:44.120 --> 00:08:45.840
[Proverbs 29: 17]

00:08:54.160 --> 00:08:55.480
[Proverbs 22:6]

00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:08.600
Now this does not mean that you should&nbsp;
be harsh with them or provoke them to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.600 --> 00:09:13.480
anger or beat them blue and purple.
That is not what God's Word says.&nbsp;

00:09:13.480 --> 00:09:20.800
But depending on their personality, you need&nbsp;
to discipline them with wisdom and love.

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:22.160
[Ephesians 6:4]

00:09:36.160 --> 00:09:42.520
You know, I was always busy and naughty,&nbsp;
so my dad, he would keep his word.&nbsp;

00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:47.400
He would give me three warnings, but if I&nbsp;
didn't listen, he said he is going to spank&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.400 --> 00:09:55.280
me after the third time, and he always did.
That gave me security - a kind of structure to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:59.120
know there's always consequences and also&nbsp;
to know that my dad will keep his word.&nbsp;

00:09:59.880 --> 00:10:03.680
And afterward, you know,&nbsp;
after I cried, he spanked me.&nbsp;

00:10:03.680 --> 00:10:10.400
He would explain to me exactly again to make&nbsp;
sure that I know why he gave me a spanking.&nbsp;

00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:16.400
What I did was wrong and I needed to&nbsp;
apologize and when I did that, he hugged me.&nbsp;

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:20.880
He told me he loves me.
The relationship is restored again.&nbsp;

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:25.480
Father - son.
And then I continued, but I learned my lesson.&nbsp;

00:10:25.480 --> 00:10:30.040
Those three warnings gave me structure - security.
There are a lot of people who scream at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.040 --> 00:10:33.760
their kids and they threaten them.
Seven, eight, nine, ten times - if you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.760 --> 00:10:39.480
do this again I'm going to do this and that and&nbsp;
you don't do that and so there's no structure.&nbsp;

00:10:39.480 --> 00:10:41.880
Sometimes you say it three times.
Sometimes 15.&nbsp;

00:10:41.880 --> 00:10:46.000
So that means you don't keep your word.
If you say to your child - if you do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:50.160
this again I am going to discipline you -&nbsp;
then you need to keep your word and do it.&nbsp;

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:55.200
They need that structure to know that&nbsp;
when you say something as their parent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:59.960
that you will do what you said you will do.
There's a difference between being a friend&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.960 --> 00:11:07.120
to your child which you also need to be and then&nbsp;
that authority where they learn respect for you.

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:08.400
[Hebrews 12:11]

00:11:22.440 --> 00:11:26.320
You know, some parents are&nbsp;
against disciplining their kids.&nbsp;

00:11:26.320 --> 00:11:31.520
And you can just see how those kids - they&nbsp;
have no respect for their parents - but they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.520 --> 00:11:40.120
then scream at their kids - scream and loud,&nbsp;
you know, psychological abuse is a lot worse.

00:11:40.120 --> 00:11:41.640
[Colossians 3:21]

00:11:49.040 --> 00:11:54.680
So, discipline your children in love.
If they did something bad after you warn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:54.680 --> 00:12:00.280
them a few times, let's say the third time, you&nbsp;
discipline them and just don't leave it there.&nbsp;

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:02.520
Just don't discipline them and walk away.
No.&nbsp;

00:12:02.520 --> 00:12:09.480
Talk to them, have a conversation, make sure they&nbsp;
understand why you discipline them and tell them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:09.480 --> 00:12:13.080
to apologize and then give them a hug.
Give them a kiss.&nbsp;

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:15.760
Restore that relationship.
And then you continue.&nbsp;

00:12:15.760 --> 00:12:20.440
You need to do that in the same&nbsp;
way that God is now your Father.&nbsp;

00:12:20.440 --> 00:12:23.120
You are His child.
And so when you go and you do something bad,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:23.120 --> 00:12:29.040
you come back and you say you're sorry.
He forgives you, and you continue.&nbsp;

00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:32.640
Say sorry.
Apologize.&nbsp;

00:12:32.640 --> 00:12:36.520
Ask forgiveness.
It's not just your kids who need to apologize.&nbsp;

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:39.640
And ask you for forgiveness&nbsp;
when they do something wrong.&nbsp;

00:12:39.640 --> 00:12:45.160
You need to set the example.
There's no such thing as a perfect father.&nbsp;

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:48.600
We all know that.
You will make mistakes and then they look&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:48.600 --> 00:12:53.760
at you - your kids they look at how you act.
So you can't expect them to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:53.760 --> 00:12:58.840
say sorry if you don't do it.
So if you did something wrong, own that mistake.&nbsp;

00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:02.360
Apologize.
Ask them to forgive you.&nbsp;

00:13:02.360 --> 00:13:06.920
Never just ignore it because if&nbsp;
you do, your kids will do the same.

00:13:06.920 --> 00:13:08.760
[James 5:16]

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:19.040
You know, my dad would always do this.
And for a lot of men this might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:19.040 --> 00:13:24.440
be difficult because of pride.
They wrongly think that if they do this - if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:24.440 --> 00:13:30.280
they apologize to their kids - then they would&nbsp;
think less of them and that's because of pride.&nbsp;

00:13:30.280 --> 00:13:33.280
The sinful flesh.
It's actually the opposite.&nbsp;

00:13:33.280 --> 00:13:37.080
For example, my dad would come&nbsp;
if he and my mom had words.&nbsp;

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:42.600
For example, in the kitchen and we were there we&nbsp;
saw this conversation, he would come back later&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:42.600 --> 00:13:48.040
and he would apologize to her and also to us.
He would say something like, you know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:48.040 --> 00:13:52.840
even if what I said was right, the way&nbsp;
I spoke to your mother was not right.&nbsp;

00:13:52.840 --> 00:13:56.960
Please forgive me.
And then we would and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:56.960 --> 00:14:05.120
that made me respect him so so much more.
And that example helps even me today in my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:05.120 --> 00:14:12.640
marriage and with all other relationships - to own&nbsp;
my mistakes - to say I am sorry when I'm wrong.&nbsp;

00:14:12.640 --> 00:14:16.160
It's easy not to do it - to just ignore it, right?
That's easy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:16.160 --> 00:14:21.000
because it's part of the sinful flesh.
But it's through the spirit that you will go and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:26.800
make things right between you and your family.
Own your mistakes, set that example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:30.880
and your kids will follow.
There will be this openness - this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:30.880 --> 00:14:37.720
beautiful love - where people are humble and&nbsp;
there's no place for sin or the devil to creep&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:37.720 --> 00:14:47.320
in and break up that family because of pride.
Put your family first - not yourself or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:49.680
other things.
Put them first.&nbsp;

00:14:49.680 --> 00:14:56.040
It's one of the reasons I loved my dad so much.
You know, he would he would give his last money&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:56.040 --> 00:15:02.120
or take off his clothes just so that&nbsp;
we could go and study and get degrees.&nbsp;

00:15:02.120 --> 00:15:06.880
He did everything for us and he&nbsp;
didn't even think about it twice.&nbsp;

00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:12.400
There were so many things that&nbsp;
he sacrificed from his own life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:12.400 --> 00:15:20.920
that now that he passed away I'm starting to&nbsp;
remember things and I appreciate it so much.

00:15:20.920 --> 00:15:22.160
[Philippians 2:3]

00:15:38.920 --> 00:15:44.160
Pride and selfishness can always&nbsp;
come between you and your kids.&nbsp;

00:15:44.160 --> 00:15:48.120
It will prevent you from&nbsp;
having a good relationship.&nbsp;

00:15:48.120 --> 00:15:52.240
For example, pride stops&nbsp;
you from asking forgiveness.&nbsp;

00:15:52.240 --> 00:15:55.280
Selfishness prevents you from&nbsp;
putting your children up as one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:55.280 --> 00:16:00.760
of the highest priorities in your life.
And ignorance stops you from spending&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:00.760 --> 00:16:08.640
enough quality time with them because&nbsp;
you think they need your money more.&nbsp;

00:16:08.640 --> 00:16:14.960
You know, as a reborn Christian, you have the&nbsp;
Holy Spirit in you, which means loving them.&nbsp;

00:16:14.960 --> 00:16:16.440
Your family.
It's not just when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:16.440 --> 00:16:22.640
you want to - it's an act of your will.
It's agape love, unconditional love.&nbsp;

00:16:22.640 --> 00:16:26.240
There's storge love as well and&nbsp;
philia, which means there's friendship&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:26.240 --> 00:16:29.480
love and family love, right?
Eros love is sexual love and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:29.480 --> 00:16:34.960
that comes only together with your wife, right?
But all the others, is with you and your kids.&nbsp;

00:16:34.960 --> 00:16:40.920
And you need to do that always, even when you&nbsp;
see your children need to spend time with you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:40.920 --> 00:16:45.280
even when you're tired and don't feel like it.
There are moments in your life when you need&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:45.280 --> 00:16:49.360
to sacrifice your own feelings&nbsp;
and give them what they need.&nbsp;

00:16:49.360 --> 00:16:54.520
And the moment you put on that switch, when you&nbsp;
act through the Spirit, you will suddenly see that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:54.520 --> 00:16:58.640
your whole soul - your emotions - your intellect&nbsp;
- your own will - just comes together and now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:58.640 --> 00:17:02.000
you want to spend time with them.
You know, my dad did not always&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:05.040
have a lot of money.
But he tried his best&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:12.000
even though he was very busy to always take&nbsp;
time and spend time with us as his kids.&nbsp;

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:17.240
We are five kids - five very different&nbsp;
personalities - and he tried to connect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:17.240 --> 00:17:21.840
with each one of us on our level&nbsp;
with our different personality.&nbsp;

00:17:21.840 --> 00:17:29.800
Your children should not learn to become a great&nbsp;
man or woman from school or from their friends.&nbsp;

00:17:29.800 --> 00:17:35.520
They learn it from you.
Their identity - they get that from you.&nbsp;

00:17:35.520 --> 00:17:43.680
Money - it's going to make things worse.
They need you - time with you - and if you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:43.680 --> 00:17:49.360
don't spend time with them, how are you going&nbsp;
to know what they truly need and how to spend&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:49.360 --> 00:17:52.160
time with them specifically?
And how are you going to put&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:52.160 --> 00:17:56.200
them first in your life - truly?
Let me ask you a few questions.&nbsp;

00:17:56.200 --> 00:18:02.680
Do you even know the favorite colors of your kids?
What are their favorite hobbies?&nbsp;

00:18:02.680 --> 00:18:04.800
What do they like?
What don't they like?&nbsp;

00:18:04.800 --> 00:18:10.080
And do they know those things of you?
Do they know you?&nbsp;

00:18:10.080 --> 00:18:13.920
Make time for your kids.
Time passes so quick... and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:13.920 --> 00:18:21.400
one of these days they'll be mature and&nbsp;
then when you look back in your life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:21.400 --> 00:18:25.920
those thoughts would come and you would think,&nbsp;
man, I should have spent more time with them.&nbsp;

00:18:25.920 --> 00:18:28.520
I should have gone more fishing.
I should have done this more.&nbsp;

00:18:28.520 --> 00:18:31.480
I should have done that more.
Well, now you still have time.&nbsp;

00:18:31.480 --> 00:18:36.680
You can't go back right now into the past,&nbsp;
but you have time to do things right now.&nbsp;

00:18:36.680 --> 00:18:43.800
So act now and don't wait for regret.
Let's move on to the next one.&nbsp;

00:18:43.800 --> 00:18:49.920
Number five: Love them and make&nbsp;
sure that they know you love them.&nbsp;

00:18:49.920 --> 00:18:54.000
You know, my dad wasn't a perfect father&nbsp;
because there's no such thing, as we said&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:54.000 --> 00:18:57.360
at the beginning of this video.
But he was near because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:57.360 --> 00:19:00.560
he lived the way he preached.
When he made mistakes, he would come back,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:00.560 --> 00:19:04.480
ask forgiveness and make it right.
And he would always make sure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:04.480 --> 00:19:11.760
that we know that he loved us.
Do your kids know that you love them?&nbsp;

00:19:11.760 --> 00:19:15.800
They're not going to know it through&nbsp;
you buying them gifts or taking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:15.800 --> 00:19:21.960
them fishing or doing other things for them.
They might even get too spoiled and not appreciate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:21.960 --> 00:19:26.920
things enough if you always just give them stuff.
You need to tell them you love&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:26.920 --> 00:19:30.680
them from your lips.
They need to hear it.&nbsp;

00:19:30.680 --> 00:19:35.720
Some parents might be a little bit hesitant or&nbsp;
afraid, you know, if they are going to be too&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:35.720 --> 00:19:41.720
strict - or not strict - but tell them don't do&nbsp;
this, don't do that, then they might think you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:41.720 --> 00:19:44.160
don't love them anymore.
No.&nbsp;

00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:48.640
You love them if you discipline them.
You can tell them the truth of certain things when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:48.640 --> 00:19:53.360
they go off the right path, you know. They make&nbsp;
their own decisions, especially when they grow up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:53.360 --> 00:19:58.480
and then you leave them but you still tell&nbsp;
them this is right - this is wrong - with love.&nbsp;

00:19:58.480 --> 00:20:02.440
And when you tell them that, they should&nbsp;
never feel that you don't love them anymore.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:02.440 --> 00:20:06.840
That you don't care about them.
God our Father is a good example.&nbsp;

00:20:06.840 --> 00:20:11.240
He loves us and we know it.
But He doesn't love our sin.

00:20:11.240 --> 00:20:12.360
[Romans 5:8]

00:20:23.800 --> 00:20:25.920
Love them and keep on praying for them.&nbsp;

00:20:25.920 --> 00:20:29.760
Always let them know that&nbsp;
you're praying for them as well.&nbsp;

00:20:29.760 --> 00:20:33.120
You know, my story was like&nbsp;
the story of the prodigal son.&nbsp;

00:20:33.120 --> 00:20:37.880
I knew my parents loved me and I also&nbsp;
knew that they were praying for me.&nbsp;

00:20:37.880 --> 00:20:41.600
I went away but you know God was&nbsp;
working in me and I think it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:41.600 --> 00:20:47.640
because of those prayers and I came back.
So let them know that you pray for them.&nbsp;

00:20:47.640 --> 00:20:51.640
Do not quarrel unnecessarily with your kids.
Always tell them, oh don't do this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:51.640 --> 00:20:53.680
don't do this, don't do this.
Show them love as well.&nbsp;

00:20:53.680 --> 00:20:57.680
There needs to be a balance.
Tell them the truth in love&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:57.680 --> 00:21:04.120
but then continue the relationship with them as&nbsp;
well so that they will know that you love them.&nbsp;

00:21:04.120 --> 00:21:10.080
God gave them free will to make their own&nbsp;
decisions so let them make their own decisions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:10.080 --> 00:21:15.120
as God lets you make your own decisions.
But we know what God's Word says.&nbsp;

00:21:15.120 --> 00:21:19.720
We know what He wants from us, and it's&nbsp;
the same thing with you and your kids.&nbsp;

00:21:19.720 --> 00:21:25.360
You tell them this is right, this is wrong.
But then, when they get that certain age,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:25.360 --> 00:21:28.040
you kind of have to let them go.
When they leave the nest.&nbsp;

00:21:28.720 --> 00:21:32.520
But never stop to be a good example.
And always pray for them.

00:21:32.520 --> 00:21:33.960
[1 Timothy 2:8]

00:21:45.040 --> 00:21:46.840
[1 Thessalonians 5:17]

00:21:50.480 --> 00:21:51.720
[James 5:16]

00:21:58.760 --> 00:22:03.280
Now remember, there is no such&nbsp;
thing as a perfect father.&nbsp;

00:22:03.280 --> 00:22:11.040
Only God the Father - He is a perfect father.
And we can try our best to follow His example.&nbsp;

00:22:11.040 --> 00:22:17.640
Now, go and be a great father, and&nbsp;
always remember, that life is short.&nbsp;

00:22:17.640 --> 00:22:23.400
So don't waste yours, because what will&nbsp;
your kids think of you when you're not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:23.400 --> 00:22:27.520
here anymore?
Cheers guys.

